  "query_preview": "..\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nTonight through Saturday: an upper level ridge moves across the \nregion bringing warmer and drier weather. A gusty SE wind is \nexpected ahead of a cold front Saturday night, that has prompted\nthe issuance of a Lake Wind Advisory. This in effect from 9 am\nSaturday till 3 am Sunday.\n\nSaturday night through Monday: Conditions will be cool and mainly\nwetter than normal as an upper low drifts east from the Canadian \nRockies. No widespread organized severe thunderstorms are\nexpected, but an isolated brief strong storm is possible.\n\nTuesday onward: Conditions dry out and warm as the upper low moves\nout. Expect high temps Friday to reach the 80s across most of the\nCWA.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nBlended Near-term models in for forecast Sky grids. Otherwise, default\nNBM was used. TFJ",
